# SignFlow AI

### Real-Time Continuous Indian Sign Language (ISL) to English Translation

[![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/status-in--development-orange)](#project-status)
[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.11%2B-blue)](#technology-stack)
[![React](https://img.shields.io/badge/React-TypeScript-61DAFB)](#technology-stack)
[![FastAPI](https://img.shields.io/badge/FastAPI-Backend-009688)](#technology-stack)
[![PyTorch](https://img.shields.io/badge/PyTorch-Deep%20Learning-EE4C2C)](#technology-stack)
[![MediaPipe](https://img.shields.io/badge/MediaPipe-Computer%20Vision-4285F4)](#technology-stack)

> **SignFlow AI is a portfolio-oriented research prototype that converts continuous Indian Sign Language video into an intermediate sign/gloss sequence, translates that sequence into natural English, and optionally produces speech.**

---

## 1. Project Overview

Traditional gesture-recognition applications often classify one static hand gesture at a time.

For example:

```text
Hand gesture → A
Hand gesture → B
Hand gesture → C
```

That is useful for alphabet recognition, but it is not enough for **continuous sign-language understanding**.

SignFlow AI is designed around a more advanced pipeline:

```text
Continuous ISL Video
        ↓
Hand + Pose + Facial Landmark Extraction
        ↓
Feature Normalization
        ↓
Temporal Sequence Construction
        ↓
Deep Learning Temporal Model
        ↓
Gloss / Sign Sequence
        ↓
English Language Normalization
        ↓
English Text
        ↓
Optional Text-to-Speech
```

The project is intentionally developed as a **bounded-vocabulary continuous-translation prototype**. It is not intended to claim unrestricted or perfect translation of all Indian Sign Language.

---

# 2. Problem Statement

People who use Indian Sign Language may face communication barriers when interacting with people who do not know sign language.

A useful assistive system should be able to:

- observe signing through a camera,
- understand movement across time,
- identify a sequence of signs rather than a single pose,
- produce readable text,
- optionally produce speech,
- operate with low enough latency for interactive use.

The challenge is that sign-language meaning can depend on:

- hand shape,
- hand orientation,
- hand location,
- movement,
- interaction between both hands,
- body pose,
- facial cues,
- temporal context.

Therefore, SignFlow AI treats sign recognition as a **spatiotemporal sequence-learning problem** rather than a simple image-classification problem.

---

# 3. Project Goals

## Primary Goal

Build a web-based AI system that can process continuous ISL signing and generate a readable English sentence.

## Secondary Goals

1. Build a real-time webcam interface.
2. Extract structured hand, pose, and facial features.
3. Train a temporal sequence model.
4. Support a controlled ISL vocabulary.
5. Produce an intermediate gloss/sign representation.
6. Translate glosses into natural English.
7. Provide optional speech output.
8. Expose model confidence and latency.
9. Evaluate recognition and translation performance.
10. Document the complete system as a professional GitHub portfolio project.

---

# 4. Example

Suppose the signer continuously performs a sequence corresponding to:

```text
ME → NAME → ARJUN
```

The system should ideally produce:

```text
Gloss:
ME NAME ARJUN

English:
My name is Arjun.
```

Another example:

```text
Gloss:
I WANT GO COLLEGE

English:
I want to go to college.
```

The important point is that the application works with a **sequence** rather than requiring a separate prediction-and-click action for every sign.

---

# 5. What Makes This a Level-3 Project?

There are three useful project levels:

### Level 1 — Static Gesture Recognition

```text
Image → One gesture
```

Example:

```text
Hand → A
```

### Level 2 — Word / Isolated Sign Recognition

```text
Video clip → One sign
```

Example:

```text
Video → HELLO
```

### Level 3 — Continuous Sign Recognition / Translation

```text
Continuous video
        ↓
Sign sequence
        ↓
Language representation
        ↓
English sentence
```

SignFlow AI targets **Level 3** for its portfolio architecture.

---

# 6. Important Scope Definition

A 30-day project cannot realistically cover every ISL sign, every signer, every regional variation, and unrestricted natural-language translation.

Therefore, the initial release uses:

```text
Controlled vocabulary
        +
Short continuous phrases / sentences
        +
Research/public datasets where permitted
        +
Project-specific test recordings
```

The project should be described as:

> **Continuous ISL recognition and translation for a defined vocabulary and evaluation setting.**

Avoid describing it as:

> "A universal Indian Sign Language translator."

That distinction is important for technical accuracy.

---

