# 25. Dataset Strategy

The data strategy should combine research resources and controlled project data.

## Public Research Data

A particularly relevant resource is:

### ISLTranslate

The ISLTranslate dataset was introduced for Indian Sign Language to English translation and contains **31,222 ISL-English sentence/phrase pairs**.

Paper:

> Joshi, A., Agrawal, S., & Modi, A. (2023). *ISLTranslate: Dataset for Translating Indian Sign Language*. Findings of ACL 2023.

Reference:

```text
https://aclanthology.org/2023.findings-acl.665/
```

## iSign

The iSign research ecosystem provides resources for Indian Sign Language video/pose-to-text tasks and is useful for understanding larger-scale continuous sign-language research.

Repository:

```text
https://github.com/Exploration-Lab/iSign
```

## ISLRTC

The Indian Sign Language Research and Training Centre (ISLRTC) provides official ISL resources, including an ISL Dictionary.

Official site:

```text
https://islrtc.nic.in/
```

Review dataset/resource licenses and usage conditions before redistribution, training, or commercial deployment.

---

# 26. Controlled Vocabulary

The first working release should use a manageable set of signs.

Possible categories:

### Greetings

```text
HELLO
GOOD
WELCOME
THANK
SORRY
```

### Identity

```text
I
YOU
MY
YOUR
NAME
```

### Actions

```text
GO
COME
WANT
NEED
HELP
EAT
DRINK
```

### Places

```text
HOME
SCHOOL
COLLEGE
OFFICE
```

### Time

```text
TODAY
TOMORROW
YESTERDAY
NOW
```

The actual vocabulary should be selected based on the dataset and the signs that can be trained and evaluated reliably.

---

# 27. Data Collection Strategy

A custom collection tool should be created early in the project.

Example:

```text
Select Sign:
[ GO ▼ ]

Samples:
[ 000 / 500 ]

┌─────────────────────────┐
│                         │
│       LIVE CAMERA       │
│                         │
└─────────────────────────┘

[ START RECORDING ]
```

Pipeline:

```text
Camera
  ↓
Frames
  ↓
Landmarks
  ↓
Normalized features
  ↓
Sequence
  ↓
Dataset file
```

For custom evaluation data, collect samples from multiple people where possible and obtain appropriate consent.

---

# 28. Recommended Dataset Split

Avoid only doing a random frame split when video clips from the same signer appear in both training and testing.

Prefer a signer-aware split:

```text
TRAIN
Signers A, B, C, D...

VALIDATION
Signers E...

TEST
Signers F...
```

This provides a more useful estimate of how the system handles a signer it has not seen during training.

---

# 29. Evaluation

Do not judge the project only by accuracy.

## Sign / Token Metrics

- Accuracy
- Precision
- Recall
- F1-score

## Continuous Translation

- Word Error Rate (WER)
- Sequence accuracy
- Edit distance

## Real-Time Performance

- FPS
- Average inference latency
- End-to-end latency
- Dropped frames
- CPU/GPU utilization

## Robustness

Test:

```text
Different lighting
Different backgrounds
Different camera distances
Different signers
Left/right hand differences
Slow signing
Fast signing
Partial occlusion
No-hand frames
Unsupported signs
```

---

# 30. Experiment Tracking

Every major experiment should record:

```text
Experiment ID
Dataset version
Vocabulary size
Feature representation
Sequence length
Window stride
Model
Hidden dimension
Number of layers
Learning rate
Batch size
Epochs
Optimizer
Validation metrics
Test metrics
Latency
Hardware
Notes
```

Example:

```text
Experiment: EXP-007
Model: Transformer
Input: Hand + Pose + Face
Sequence: 48 frames
Vocabulary: 50 signs
Optimizer: AdamW
Learning rate: <measured setting>
WER: <measured value>
F1: <measured value>
Latency: <measured value>
```

Never publish invented accuracy, F1, or WER values.

