# 45. Interview Explanation

### What problem does your project solve?

> SignFlow AI is designed to reduce communication barriers by translating continuous Indian Sign Language signing into English text and optional speech.

### Why not classify individual frames?

> A single frame captures hand configuration but not movement over time. Continuous signing requires temporal information, so the system constructs feature sequences and uses a temporal deep-learning model.

### Why landmarks?

> Landmarks provide a structured representation of hand, body, and facial information and can reduce the visual complexity of the learning problem compared with feeding every raw frame directly to a large video model.

### Why BiLSTM?

> BiLSTM provides a strong baseline for sequence modeling and gives us a simpler architecture against which to compare a Transformer.

### Why Transformer?

> The Transformer allows attention across different temporal positions, making it useful for modeling relationships across a sign sequence.

### Why a gloss layer?

> It separates visual recognition from language generation. This makes the pipeline easier to evaluate, debug, and improve independently.

### Why WER?

> Continuous translation is a sequence prediction task, so Word Error Rate is useful for measuring differences between predicted and reference word sequences.

### Is it a complete ISL translator?

> No. The first release is a bounded-vocabulary continuous translation prototype. It is designed to demonstrate the architecture and engineering pipeline rather than claim unrestricted human-level interpretation.

